                    {
                        "form_id": "1f53447f-61c3-423f-b10e-1de5f886c70a",
                        "entry_id": "3ad07ba9-414b-3fe5-9c1f-67d959aca68d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "рукоплеска́ниях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d1e975ee-e637-3039-880c-7ffa7447e2d9",
                        "entry_id": "3ad07ba9-414b-3fe5-9c1f-67d959aca68d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "то же, что рукоплескания; хлопки в ладоши в знак одобрения, приветствия; аплодисменты"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "487b936c-cc08-4488-b756-d8edfd334796",
                                "sense_id": "d1e975ee-e637-3039-880c-7ffa7447e2d9",
                                "text": "И если тебе импонирует рукоплескание площади, следует понимать, что твои побуждения, твое поведение оцениваются уже по особу счету."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "576f8034-8898-4113-879c-65a2ecd8032c",
                                "sense_id": "d1e975ee-e637-3039-880c-7ffa7447e2d9",
                                "text": "Вторая лекция была поразительно хороша, и на третьей он был встречен единодушным рукоплесканием…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d8437d86-9c97-4610-a632-ec5ec7f89cd4",
                        "source_entry_id": "3ad07ba9-414b-3fe5-9c1f-67d959aca68d",
                        "source_sense_id": "d1e975ee-e637-3039-880c-7ffa7447e2d9",
                        "target_lang_word": "applause",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "applause",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4cd6c6ed-805c-3038-a0bd-a528d04b40ae",
                                        "entry_id": "6ab18e25-016a-3e5e-9e88-f4ad2705af84",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of applauding; approbation and praise publicly expressed by the clapping of hands, stamping or tapping of the feet, acclamation, huzzas, or other means; marked commendation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9fb97a9c-90a7-4745-bde8-10b6757c1bf0",
                                                "sense_id": "4cd6c6ed-805c-3038-a0bd-a528d04b40ae",
                                                "text": "A few days before, the adulations and applauses of a nation were sounding in her [Marie Louise, Duchess of Parma's] ears, and now she was come to this!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a20e275-07ae-42ff-86ad-c9065f68d93a",
                                                "sense_id": "4cd6c6ed-805c-3038-a0bd-a528d04b40ae",
                                                "text": "Lestrade and I sat silent for a moment, and then, with a spontaneous impulse, we both broke at clapping, as at the well-wrought crisis of a play. […] It was at such moments that for an instant he [Sherlock Holmes] ceased to be a reasoning machine, and betrayed his human love for admiration and applause."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d89dab6f-16ed-48ae-9dd2-520f1ae3d5f8",
                                                "sense_id": "4cd6c6ed-805c-3038-a0bd-a528d04b40ae",
                                                "text": "Livy never gets her share of those applauses, but it is because the people do not know. Yet she is entitled to the lion's share."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50a7de32-bd18-43ee-a7c5-fc79742c1c58",
                                                "sense_id": "4cd6c6ed-805c-3038-a0bd-a528d04b40ae",
                                                "text": "Rice’s celebrations upon his goal were controlled, muted. Not so those of Grealish, who lapped up the applause of the England fans behind the goal."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "applause",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e4f5ad01-c4c3-3359-a962-217d7c26f07e",
                                        "entry_id": "eb496836-4b36-3535-ade0-8fe1c60a3df3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To applaud."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8df8a5b5-0ee0-42ad-afcb-1c3a1ad56398",
                                                "sense_id": "e4f5ad01-c4c3-3359-a962-217d7c26f07e",
                                                "text": "But (which had ſcarrefide our wounds, if wounded, with the Balme / Of her ſweete Preſence, ſo applaus’d as in Sea-ſtormes a Calme) / Her royall-ſelfe, Elizabeth our Soueraigne lawfull Queene, / In magnanimious Maieſtie amidſt her Troupes was ſeene."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "63616e77-29b1-4a9c-a7a3-b2146afb9f27",
                                                "sense_id": "e4f5ad01-c4c3-3359-a962-217d7c26f07e",
                                                "text": "Now Ahab ſees the ground of that applauſed conſent of his rabble of Prophets: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a00905d-1ee1-4775-b9f2-5277559fcbac",
                                                "sense_id": "e4f5ad01-c4c3-3359-a962-217d7c26f07e",
                                                "text": "O ſacred Emperour, theſe ears have heard, / What no Sons ears can unrevenged hear, / The Princes all of them, but ſpecially, / The Prince Elector Archbiſhop of Collen, / Revil’d him by the names of murderer, / Arch villain, robber of the Empires fame, / And Cæſars tutor in all wickedneſs, / And with a general voice applaus’d his death, / As for a ſpecial good to Chriſtendome."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
